WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:08.180
Let's go to the 4 0 8 area code caller from
4 0 8.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.450
What's your name where you're calling from?

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.790
This is Logan from Saturday.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Hey, Logan, what's up?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.450
I actually have another question on voter
turnout.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:26.680
So with the, you know, all the Corona virus
restrictions in the social distance thing,

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.040
I'm hoping that stuff gets, you know, a lot
of it gets cleared up by November.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.460
But I like the.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.440
The after effects of it are going to last
longer, you know, people are going to go out

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.050
as much and you know, I'm just wondering.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.980
I think there is going to be a lower voter
turnout in November.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.120
But do you think that's good?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.330
You know, historically, a lower verdict.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.010
Voter turnout disproportionately hurts Democrats.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.329
But do you think that's gonna be the case
or is it going to be more of an across the

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:53.010
board lower turnout?

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:57.650
You know, if you put a gun to my head and
say you've got a bet on it, my bet is that

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:02.070
the virus will impact voter turnout in November
in a way that helps Trump.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:08.000
And the reason why I say that is Democrats
are taking the virus much more seriously than

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Republicans.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.830
Democrats are social distancing, much more
than Republicans.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:20.140
So no matter what happens, my instinct is
there will be more Democrats who opt not to

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.560
go out in public in a large crowd at voting
locations than Republicans who will do that.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.130
So I believe that the voter turnout dynamics
in November are going to be beneficial to

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.130
Donald Trump.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.590
I want to be wrong and we need to work to
make that not be the case.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:37.770
I think we should go to 100 percent absentee
ballot voting by mail.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:41.640
But I think if we just have a normal everybody
shows up to vote on November 6th, I think

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.729
it helps Trump.

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:44.110
Right, right.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:50.119
And, you know, it's obviously unprecedented,
so it's pretty hard to predict kind of shot

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:51.119
in the dark there.

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:52.119
Yeah.

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:55.010
All we can look at is on this during the social
distancing more seriously.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.280
And that's what makes me think that.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.470
OK.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.659
Well, one other quick question on what I've
been thinking a little bit more about why

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:10.300
Bernie didn't do so well in the in the primary,
and I listen to some of your commentary saying

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.900
that, you know, the progressive platform isn't
necessarily as popular as Reddit and Twitter

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.900
would make you breathe.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.900
And that's, you know, being young.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:17.900
That's right.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:18.900
I do spend a lot of my time.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.989
So I was a little disappointed there.

00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:26.239
But my question is, you know, moving forward,
maybe just that the next election, do you

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:31.749
think it would be beneficial for a progressive
candidate to kind of hone in, focus on on

00:02:31.749 --> 00:02:33.629
one piece of the platform?

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:35.670
And naturally, that would be Medicare for
all?

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:40.939
Because I think that's the most popular and
can present a more, I guess, moderate stance

00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:43.689
on some of the other progressive topics.

00:02:43.689 --> 00:02:47.419
I don't know that I would say I don't know
that it's about being more moderate in some

00:02:47.419 --> 00:02:49.349
areas and more progressive in other areas.

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:53.219
I think it's just about the framing and PR
around the campaign.

00:02:53.219 --> 00:02:56.590
You can be progressive in five important areas.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.620
But there is strategy, understanding where
you are running and your constituents to know

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.829
which one is more important.

00:03:02.829 --> 00:03:04.329
So let me give you an example.

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:12.000
If you're in a very, very heavy union area
with manufacturing, for example, I don't fall

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.629
for this stuff.

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:14.949
Everybody loves their health plan.

00:03:14.949 --> 00:03:21.519
But it is true that there are lots of unionized
workers who are satisfied with the health

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:26.989
care that they have because they've done collective
bargaining and they have something way better

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:31.079
than what lots of other people have in a place
like that.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:37.279
You might want to focus more on maybe it's
minimum wage, maybe it's workers rights, maybe

00:03:37.279 --> 00:03:43.540
it's education rather than maybe Medicare
for all, because you understand your constituency

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:49.060
where it is less of an issue for them to go
to Medicare for all because they like what

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.879
their union may have been able to negotiate
for them.

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:54.569
That doesn't mean you change your position
on Medicare for all.

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:57.909
It just means that maybe in your district
you campaign a little differently.

00:03:57.909 --> 00:03:59.219
Does that make sense?

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:00.219
Yeah.

00:04:00.219 --> 00:04:01.219
Yeah.

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:04.219
He just kind of tailored the message to whoever
the audience is.

00:04:04.219 --> 00:04:05.219
Right.

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:06.219
Exactly.

00:04:06.219 --> 00:04:07.219
Exactly.

00:04:07.219 --> 00:04:10.290
Doesn't mean you compromise on your values
or your positions, but the focus of your campaign

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.109
may be affected.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:13.109
OK.

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:17.373
Last night I got for you today, I appreciate
you taking my call.

00:04:17.373 --> 00:04:18.373
All right.

00:04:18.373 --> 00:04:19.373
Thank you.

00:04:19.373 --> 00:04:20.373
I appreciate you calling in.

00:04:20.373 --> 00:04:20.378
Great to hear from you.

